// # oodar/qa — Substrate Self-Tests
//
// Logline: The v2.2.0+ qa/ subdir holds 2 test utilities (dudect_c_native, oo_hip_so_smoke) + 5 tier-5 tests_challenger_*.c files that exercise the 8D Red Team matrix (per openOODA/practices/8d-red-team.oot).
//
// Setup: Self-tests ship with the package. The 2 utilities are smoke / benchmark tests; the 5 challenger tests are adversarial / regression probes. The umbrella TU (oodar.c) EXCLUDES the qa/ subdir — these are run by the developer, not the runtime.
//
// Beats:
//   1. dudect_c_native.c     — Welch t-test probe (Red 8 dim 7, benchmark).
//   2. oo_hip_so_smoke.c     — HIP/ROCm kernel load smoke (Red 8 dim 1, functional).
//   3. tests_challenger_cap_escape.c         — cap system bypass attempt (Red 8 dim 2+8, adversarial).
//   4. tests_challenger_dudect_ct.c          — constant-time dudect probe (Red 8 dim 7, benchmark).
//   5. tests_challenger_cap_threat.c         — cap-threat containment (Red 8 dim 2+8, adversarial).
//   6. tests_challenger_sandbox_containment.c — Landlock containment (Red 8 dim 2+8, redteam).
//   7. tests_challenger_proc_mem_leak.c      — proc_mem Landlock-APPLIED gate (Red 8 dim 6, regression).
//
// ──▓▓ oodar/qa ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: 2 utilities + 5 tier-5 challenger tests — 789 lines, all <= 256 ::
